WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.250
Breathe in.

2
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.290
Your chest gets bigger, and
air rushes into your lungs.

3
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.470
Breathe out, and the
air rushes back out.

4
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.190
Your body needs the
oxygen in that air.

5
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.690
So is breathing how your
body releases energy?

6
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.410
Or does the energy come
from somewhere else?

7
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.890
In this mission, you'll
see how your lungs,

8
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.970
with their tiny air sacs,
are built for swapping gases.

9
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.270
You'll use a simple model to
show what makes air rush in.

10
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.050
And you'll see what
smoking does to the lungs.

11
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.230
Your mission: find out where
your body releases its energy.
